{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgycs0dynf","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"/workspaces switcher: drop ghost paths AND exclude git worktrees (gitdir-FILE predicate)","summary":"GET /workspaces (routes/meta.js) now filters the switcher list with three predicates per path: fs.existsSync(p) && fs.existsSync(path.join(p,'.graph')) && NOT a git worktree. Worktree exclusion keys on .git being a FILE (the gitdir-pointer `git worktree add` writes) vs a DIRECTORY in a primary checkout — verified empirically: D:\\zonoid\\.git is a dir (IsDir True, kept), an orch/attempt worktree .git is a file (IsDir False, dropped). statSync throws for a non-repo workspace and the catch falls through to allow, so a legitimate primary workspace is never dropped. Rationale: orch/attempt|feature worktrees accumulate in graphStore via ?workspace= reads but must not pollute the user-facing switcher; they remain targetable via explicit ?workspace=. Also added normPath() to fold trailing seps + forward-slash variants into path.sep before the Set dedup (Windows). Stays cheap — only existsSync/statSync syscalls per path, no buildGraph.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T18:05:12.781Z","vec":[-0.0998954176902771,-0.03379236161708832,-0.01190528366714716,0.08706659823656082,0.08743545413017273,-0.07319999486207962,0.018992049619555473,0.02677685022354126,0.04047664999961853,0.08375779539346695,0.0341365709900856,0.0033233514986932278,-0.0033457637764513493,0.04067501425743103,0.002981829224154353,0.001048580277711153,0.009921683929860592,-0.0004585950227919966,0.05114401504397392,-0.05104649439454079,0.05646461248397827,0.0032683461904525757,0.004284033551812172,-0.0037062768824398518,0.07615526020526886,-0.05069504305720329,-0.08958355337381363,-0.02395511046051979,-0.05590562894940376,0.006612315308302641,-0.02108670398592949,0.032626837491989136,-0.11127866059541702,0.016581686213612556,0.07360979169607162,0.03929859399795532,0.027728553861379623,-0.06109943240880966,0.004110907204449